  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\nIntransitive ({自動詞|じどうし}). The opponent is marked with に: Xに{敗|やぶ}れる (to be defeated by X).\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{敗|やぶ}れている describes the resulting state of having been defeated.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- Xに{敗|やぶ}れる: to be defeated by X\n- Xで{敗|やぶ}れる: to lose at X (venue/round)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {試合|しあい}に{敗|やぶ}れる: to lose a match\n- {選挙|せんきょ}に{敗|やぶ}れる: to lose an election\n- {夢|ゆめ}{敗|やぶ}れる: to have one's dream shattered\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {負|ま}ける: to lose (more common in everyday speech)\n- {敗|やぶ}れる: to be defeated (more literary/formal)\n- {破|やぶ}れる: to tear, to break (different kanji, different meaning)",
